{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_145836d0beb30ca5569c3981c915713a2a8ca1fb00a7baf035bc00654046f8b2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The taste system is designed to treat every accept, reject, and edit as a signal that shapes a per-user taste profile."},{"claim_ids":["clm_213984ff31c39f425659fcedf28a2d87a39721b2a5c175a981d972d28dc8ae7f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Taste rules are designed to be shareable across a team via `npx taste push/pull`, with the README stating that rules decay while taste compounds."},{"claim_ids":["clm_24dcbcbee0c12da42c957262f707352c027c7396f5b97dbcf240ae48b137acf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README describes a model called `taste-1` as the core of the product's taste architecture, which it says learns from the user and grows with them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_34ae20392277f257008de74af2b8f58f37eee3067997cb9be87d382573626574"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A `/feedback` slash command is documented for reporting issues from within the tool, alongside GitHub issues as an alternative channel."},{"claim_ids":["clm_45e5d22019fdd444a92e0dcb68aa9ea0fd2a14026c039ecd8364160c0fd97fc2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool is distributed as the npm package `command-code`, installed with `npm i -g command-code`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_510c3efe689bfbecbc6cd41ec8fe39e9ed787ec21b8edb9b5f880657259966cc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The docs site advertises workflow recipes pairing concrete scenarios with prompts and expected outcomes, suggesting a curated usage-pattern library, though only the link is in evidence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6fbb0121b7a8f435cf25d02d7b43de1b6b6e060cc973ba6f9bec9ddc7db98863"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is a coding agent positioned as building full-stack projects, fixing bugs, writing tests, and refactoring while adapting to the user's coding style."},{"claim_ids":["clm_92d93707395d57482d26ea74abe6e78e22599b50543652e6292255078a21521e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs as a CLI: it is installed globally via npm and started inside a project with the `cmd` command."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f043110ee059a9ebdfcf68b8ee6300de8d7f94706f72ed48205b039949353c3b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Interactive sessions support typed prefixes: `/` opens a command menu, `!` enters Bash mode, and `@` triggers file-path mention autocomplete."}],"claim_ids":["clm_145836d0beb30ca5569c3981c915713a2a8ca1fb00a7baf035bc00654046f8b2","clm_213984ff31c39f425659fcedf28a2d87a39721b2a5c175a981d972d28dc8ae7f","clm_24dcbcbee0c12da42c957262f707352c027c7396f5b97dbcf240ae48b137acf6","clm_34ae20392277f257008de74af2b8f58f37eee3067997cb9be87d382573626574","clm_45e5d22019fdd444a92e0dcb68aa9ea0fd2a14026c039ecd8364160c0fd97fc2","clm_510c3efe689bfbecbc6cd41ec8fe39e9ed787ec21b8edb9b5f880657259966cc","clm_6fbb0121b7a8f435cf25d02d7b43de1b6b6e060cc973ba6f9bec9ddc7db98863","clm_92d93707395d57482d26ea74abe6e78e22599b50543652e6292255078a21521e","clm_f043110ee059a9ebdfcf68b8ee6300de8d7f94706f72ed48205b039949353c3b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:05Z","created_by_operation":"op_3b6cee990bc2441c9d1a7a8ab1fe506c","id":"pg_0d7d2f7fe3e25a35a33528c82c27c5f2","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/commandcodeai-command-code-readme-md-5c8f1b48c9d6-28c82c27c5f2.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8a967b80278f5a32a343355a1195f94f"],"title":"CommandCodeAI/command-code/readme.md @ 5c8f1b48c9d6","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:05Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3b6cee990bc2441c9d1a7a8ab1fe506c"}
